1
00:00:00,180 --> 00:00:01,530
These two spoons can be

2
00:00:01,530 --> 00:00:03,230
exactly the same temperature.

3
00:00:03,480 --> 00:00:05,140
But metal feels colder.

4
00:00:05,520 --> 00:00:06,010
How?

5
00:00:06,270 --> 00:00:07,510
Leave metal and wood

6
00:00:07,510 --> 00:00:08,790
in the same room long enough,

7
00:00:08,870 --> 00:00:10,760
and both settle
to room temperature.

8
00:00:11,293 --> 00:00:13,783
Your hand is warmer
than the spoon.

9
00:00:14,263 --> 00:00:17,183
Touch it, and heat flows
out of your skin.

10
00:00:17,533 --> 00:00:20,483
Metal carries that energy
away faster than wood.

11
00:00:21,053 --> 00:00:22,513
Same starting temperature.

12
00:00:22,713 --> 00:00:24,303
Different heat transfer.

13
00:00:24,383 --> 00:00:26,183
That colder feeling comes from

14
00:00:26,183 --> 00:00:27,783
your skin cooling faster.

15
00:00:28,073 --> 00:00:30,433
Wood takes heat away
more slowly.

16
00:00:30,693 --> 00:00:31,943
Your hand isn't simply reading

17
00:00:31,943 --> 00:00:33,393
the spoon's temperature.

18
00:00:33,653 --> 00:00:35,223
It's responding to heat

19
00:00:35,223 --> 00:00:36,473
leaving your skin.
